<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:16Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US voters reject AI data centres: could the backlash spread to France?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:924e4183f3c8ace7dad5dba25715b92677272789b59420e1845627097bd6a097</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:36:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261108-us-voters-reject-ai-data-centres-could-the-backlash-spread-to-france--b2902e041847.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/tech-24/20261108-us-voters-reject-ai-data-centres-could-the-backlash-spread-to-france" /><summary type="html">In Tuesday’s US midterm elections, voters weighed in on more than 40 local measures on data centres, and sided against them in all but one. With Democrats taking control of Congress in January and new governors in Texas and Georgia calling for moratoriums, the AI building boom faces its toughest political test yet.</summary><category term="Tech 24" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen's humanitarian crisis worsens</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d1be47f1ad539715d8f191e8f376beba37afece7fcb234655ba67aea7eca3d69</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:25Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:22:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens--95e6e91a4caa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-humanitarian-crisis-worsens" /><summary type="html">One month into the Yemeni government's offensive against the Iran-aligned Houthis, fighting continues to escalate along the Red Sea coast. Meanwhile, the humanitarian crisis is worsening, with hundreds of thousands of people displaced and the country facing the threat of catastrophe. Rula Amin, Senior Communications Advisor and spokesperson at UNHCR at Amman, in Jordan, shares further details.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland in shock after 6 killed in Krakow far-right shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:9def451b916fa04be63884306faa1a287bae0950e09bb43bf06622b9d21d0ab7</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:27Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:21:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting--b5967a40cc64.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/poland-in-shock-after-6-killed-in-krakow-far-right-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital. France 24 journalist Adrien Sariat reports from Poland.</summary></entry><entry><title>French skipper wins Route du Rhum</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:75bcedf2288d3d9eff1231b3100be2137e5b8520e7e5eec9e065b14091029724</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:30Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:20:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/french-skipper-wins-route-du-rhum--51e11d53f461.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/french-skipper-wins-route-du-rhum" /><summary type="html">French sailor Tom Laperche has won the Route du Rhum, setting a new record in the transatlantic yacht race. The 29-year-old crossed the finish line in Guadeloupe on his first attempt, beating the previous 2022 record by around six hours. A remarkable debut in one of sailing's toughest competitions!</summary></entry><entry><title>Mourning in Poland after mass shooting</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:012653e26d29cad1044deddd9c66ba225224ecfb6ba5b9fa16afc809d34cb014</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:33Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:18:48Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting--bd87f2f4ae08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/mourning-in-poland-after-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland has launched a terrorism investigation after a deadly shooting left six people dead and 16 injured. The 24-year-old Polish suspect was reportedly fascinated by far-right ideologies. Authorities are investigating the possible extremist motive as Krakow's main square remains sealed. Two days of national mourning have been declared for the victims.</summary></entry><entry><title>Europe will take part in US-mediated Ukraine talks in Abu Dhabi, French FM says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:66158b08fad72cc5b411b47c05953a804d7cfb1bc34325ba40a0644a5060ff17</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:37Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:16:31Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says--c38c48e4c7c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-europe-will-take-part-us-mediated-ukraine-peace-talks-abu-dhabi-french-fm-says" /><summary type="html">France will participate in the upcoming Abu Dhabi peace talks on ending the Ukraine war, Foreign Minister Jean-Noël Barrot said Sunday, adding that Europeans will be represented at the summit. The talks will take place under US mediation on Tuesday and Wednesday.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Pope Leo urges men to respect wives amid Latin American femicide crisis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b27690b467e2c2ffe5fd31c3b9acfa9391f417bbc4bf448d6e029b00ccae229</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:39Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T14:15:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america--c0353931a5d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261108-pope-leo-urges-husbands-to-respect-wives-amid-femicide-crisis-across-latin-america" /><summary type="html">Pope Leo XIV urged men to respect their wives as he wrapped up the first leg of his 12-day tour of Latin America. The region recorded nearly 20,000 instances of women being killed over the past five years alone, most of them murdered by a current or former partner.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>‘10 times more painful’: Menstrual disorders fuel calls to ban tear gas at French protests</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2e3289264df00b7f95cabe8bce56f238f3614d25fd8e68aa2de49a668052dc67</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:43Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T11:53:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/france/20261108-abnormal-menstraution-periods-fuel-calls-ban-tear-gas-french-protests-police--8bbcd54e5ada.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261108-abnormal-menstraution-periods-fuel-calls-ban-tear-gas-french-protests-police" /><summary type="html">French police have made extensive use of tear gas during protests that have roiled France in recent weeks, sometimes causing grievous injuries. Thousands of accounts of women experiencing acutely painful periods and increased bleeding are further challenging assumptions that the chemical irritant carries only minor consequences.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>2026 Dakar Youth Olympic Games: Golden Double for Senegal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a9b661315071af3d951b55bb6a79e2702f3b8a18a367f6bc7e61b2f9980672bd</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:46Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:56:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261108-2026-dakar-youth-olympic-games-golden-double-for-senegal--9648adca27a2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/sports/20261108-2026-dakar-youth-olympic-games-golden-double-for-senegal" /><summary type="html">Senegal won two gold medals in beach wrestling at the Youth Olympic Games in Dakar. Elisabeth Diatta won gold in the -55 kg category, the host country’s first gold medal at the Youth Olympic Games. Her compatriot Maguette Diop followed suit, taking gold in the -80 kg category.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Diwali: Over one billion people mark victory of light over darkness</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:78dca016f5e110db402f37595c949fd0da16b6f98162753ccd7c126d18e9ebce</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:48Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:46:37Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness--093adc3e4b15.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/diwali-over-one-billion-people-mark-victory-of-light-over-darkness" /><summary type="html">Diwali celebrations began on Sunday, with people across India and the global diaspora gathering to mark one of the most important festivals in the Hindu tradition. In Ayodhya, believed to be the birthplace of Lord Rama, the deity celebrated during the festival, festivities included performances based on the Hindu epic Ramayana, laser and light shows, live music, fireworks and drone displays.</summary></entry><entry><title>Paraguay: Senate impeached Peña rather than accept his offer to resign</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f92e77a1652a3613ceb4e38210955996a47ec64ebc7bfafcf291780eeade858d</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:52Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T10:42:59Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe_a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign--268a291e27fe.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261108-paraguay-senate-impeached-pe%C3%B1a-rather-than-accept-his-offer-to-resign" /><summary type="html">Paraguay's ousted president, Santiago Peña, has been charged over the collapse of Ueno Bank. Initially placed under house arrest, he has since been transferred to a military facility for his own safety. Nearly three million customers were locked out of their accounts after regulators seized control of the online bank. Repayments are now under way, but protests continue as customers demand access to their money. Peña denies any wrongdoing. Jack Pownall reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Middle East live: Israeli president officially tasks Eisenkot with forming government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29e2bbee681f40c5b873c0c6a0ef2d8a051f3c988d62c1fcc849f80186ab4874</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:54Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:47:36Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-ne--c83bf488fa4c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261108-middle-east-live-riyadh-financial-district-targeted-deadly-strikes-yemen-israel-eisenkot-netanyahu-coalition-government-elections" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog on Sunday officially tasked ex-military chief Gadi Eisenkot with trying to form a government after neither Eisenkot's bloc nor that or incumbent Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu won a clear majority in Israel's October 28 elections. Eisenkot now has up to six weeks to form a coalition government. Follow our liveblog for the latest developments from the Middle East.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>Donald Trump wants UFC fighters as assistants</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:512b1c3d9d01a04637d0f07fc3321c34ee0103b756733b43ed4a444b59116c5c</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:24:57Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:44:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-wants-ufc-fighters-as-assistants--97d62f3fe50d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/donald-trump-wants-ufc-fighters-as-assistants" /><summary type="html">After a series of combative press briefings between the Trump administration and journalists, the US president surprised many by reportedly offering Dana White, the head of the Ultimate Fighting Championship (UFC) and a longtime friend, the role of White House press secretary. Trump praised White as a “violent fighter and warrior”, but US media reports say he has already turned down the offer. Was it a punchy choice by the president or simply a punchline? Jack Pownall takes a closer look.</summary></entry><entry><title>Israel's Arab-led parties gain influence</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:eea82d3b6602bc8409c4c2108d7516bb42acf6e8e10dda7ec92f47dfa98dec2c</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:01Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:43:26Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence--0c9b38b79b08.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/israel-s-arab-led-parties-gain-influence" /><summary type="html">Arab-led parties have endorsed Gadi Eisenkot despite his ruling out a coalition with them. Their support is driven by a shared goal: removing Benjamin Netanyahu from power. But could these parties ultimately hold the balance of power in forming Israel's next government? Antonia Kerrigan reports.</summary></entry><entry><title>Gaza: Heavy rain inundates thousands of tents</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:d8f5b57cf157862b4c9a98bb53f4373d91a4747ee2c5b04390191c36ada5ed1c</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:03Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T09:42:03Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents--9e19bbe6af60.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gaza-heavy-rain-inundates-thousands-of-tents" /><summary type="html">Heavy rainfall has flooded thousands of tents sheltering displaced Palestinians across the Gaza Strip, including in Deir al-Balah. Residents say overflowing sewage has mixed with the floodwater, further worsening already dire living conditions. Families are struggling to salvage their belongings, building makeshift earthen barriers and trying to drain the water by hand. Many have seen essential items soaked and rendered unusable, adding to the hardship faced by those already displaced.</summary></entry><entry><title>Poland launches terrorism probe into mass shooting in Krakow</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bcaf436ea65990775d9a0299c1a9795199e5796c7c2fbb50b8d18275b964b1b3</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:06Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T08:59:56Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting--608f97551b17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261108-poland-launches-terrorism-probe-into-krakow-mass-shooting" /><summary type="html">Poland on Sunday launched a terror probe into the mass shooting in Krakow the day before, in which six people were killed and many more were injured. Authorities have said that the 24-year-old suspect, who used a semi-automatic rifle in his killing spree, was “fascinated by far-right ideologies”. He is currently in critical condition in hospital.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Tenerife honour teammate Jesus De Miguel with tearful tribute</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:29b55b66bf31223948a22cbea09d695942ca38a3d2c18be16f324de8425171b4</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:10Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T07:08:28Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261108-tenerife-tribute-football-striker-jesus-de-miguel-collision-death-cardiac-arrest-spain--6aeb5c550d76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261108-tenerife-tribute-football-striker-jesus-de-miguel-collision-death-cardiac-arrest-spain" /><summary type="html">Tenerife’s stadium filled up with thousands of mourners on Saturday where they held a tearful tribute to striker Jesus De Miguel, who passed away after colliding with a goalkeeper during a match, subsequently suffering a cardiac arrest. "To speak of you in the past tense ​is tremendously unfair," team captain Enric Gallego said.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>New Zealand's knife-edge parliamentary election delivers no clear winner</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b2ead3a765e5694fee628fa06cb5b8837eb7c95c508fb9fbce344d5ee8bf3696</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:13Z</updated><published>2026-11-08T03:01:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261108-new-zealand-election-produces-no-clear-winner-as-smaller-parties-make-record-gains--fa314d7e4925.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/asia-pacific/20261108-new-zealand-election-produces-no-clear-winner-as-smaller-parties-make-record-gains" /><summary type="html">No clear winner was produced in New Zealand’s legislative elections Saturday, setting up the two main blocs – Prime Minister Christopher Luxon's right-wing coalition and opposition leader Chris Hipkins' left-wing alliance – for weeks of political wrangling to attempt to cobble together a majority. Hipkins said that while New Zealanders had spoken, "it may take us a little bit longer to figure out exactly what it is that you've said".</summary><category term="Asia / Pacific" /></entry><entry><title>Gunman kills six in Krakow, three more bodies found at his house</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01e1e6dc4029a05ec86f1201f3ec3186392a4f81b049669d7fd05f0945f00e76</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T22:47:06Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house--dc06bdec4f54.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/gunmen-kills-six-in-krakow-three-more-bodies-found-at-his-house" /><summary type="html">A chilling new discovery in Poland, where three bodies have reportedly been found inside the Krakow gunman's home. That's in addition to six people killed and sixteen wounded when the attacker opened fire in the city's historic square. Prime Minister Donald Tusk has now declared the shooting an act of terrorism, saying Poland has never experienced anything quite like it. The 25-year-old suspect, described by authorities as holding radical far-right views, was shot by police.</summary></entry><entry><title>France beat Fiji to reclaim top spot in Nations Championship</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ad83612ca71492f05ba24d9b261e2732554bc848e298f290d8f157e81e963112</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:25:16Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T22:05:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sport/20261107-france-beat-fiji-to-reclaim-top-spot-in-nations-championship--8d7768f3115f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sport/20261107-france-beat-fiji-to-reclaim-top-spot-in-nations-championship" /><summary type="html">France trashed Fiji 54-17 on Saturday to return to the top of the northern hemisphere Nations Championship standings.</summary><category term="Sport" /></entry><entry><title>'A violent fighter and warrior': Trump offers press secretary role to UFC chief Dana White</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c8fea2af546eca41882948053862a10356a0f0022a1e41a64997b1a7d988dfb2</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T20:45:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-a-violent-fighter-and-warrior-trump-offers-press-secretary-role-to-ufc-chief-dana-white--b52c016d4787.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/americas/20261107-a-violent-fighter-and-warrior-trump-offers-press-secretary-role-to-ufc-chief-dana-white" /><summary type="html">US President Donald Trump on Saturday said he was asking mixed martial arts promoter Dana White to be the new White House press secretary. Trump has repeatedly tried to hitch his MAGA brand of politics to White's enormously successful Ultimate Fighting Championship.</summary><category term="Americas" /></entry><entry><title>France Unbowed’s Mélenchon unveils ‘A Shared Future’ manifesto ahead of 2027 presidential race</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:680443e641312e42e66ab6606ebfd8918b02e7212d4cd8a048afabaf0a45abb5</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:58:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261107-france-unbowed-s-m_lenchon-unveils-a-shared-future-manifesto-ahead-of-2027-presidential-rac--8b526a1069d5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261107-france-unbowed-s-m%C3%A9lenchon-unveils-a-shared-future-manifesto-ahead-of-2027-presidential-race" /><summary type="html">“We are facing a crisis of human civilisation. And we are going to win.”
 
A defiant Jean-Luc Mélenchon was in fighting mood today as he presented his presidential manifesto at Le Bourget, north of Paris. 
 
It is his fourth bid for the French presidency, and he has chosen a venue steeped in left-wing campaign history: the site of François Hollande's famous 2012 rally.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>🔴 Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e062d28def073a6aa444d2c972259f7eb2fa8973ea0472d51116e1c5a983830b</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:38:24Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government--bea9f93a0c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government" /></entry><entry><title>Israeli president picks Netanyahu's rival Eisenkot to try to form government</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:488bb869a0f657a42037f0cd633a178c68fb66fe79005b7757d6b230f778d0d2</id><updated>2026-11-08T15:23:21Z</updated><published>2026-11-07T19:37:14Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government--bea9f93a0c67.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261107-israeli-president-picks-netanyahu-s-rival-eisenkot-to-try-to-form-government" /><summary type="html">Israeli President Isaac Herzog picked former military chief Gadi Eisenkot to try to form a government, he said in a statement Saturday. Last month's parliamentary elections left neither Eisenkot nor Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu with a clear path to building a majority.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry></feed>
